For the past four centuries they have been heavily persecuted by the Christian sect ruling from Rome and may have met here to worship in secret.	四個世紀以來，他們始終受到羅馬治下基督教派的嚴酷迫害，或許正因如此，才選擇在此秘密聚會禮拜。
To the Gnostics, she is the Great Mother of wisdom, creator of the universe, mother and wife to the god who came after her.	對諾斯替教徒而言，她是智慧的偉大之母，宇宙的創造者，也是繼她而生之神的母親兼妻子。
Because of this belief, the Gnostics also allow women to be priests. And for this reason, the Christians in Rome particularly hate them.	正因這樣的信仰，諾斯替教也容許女性擔任祭司。也正因如此，羅馬的基督徒對他們恨之入骨。
The only statue present in the catacombs is that of Aphrodite.	地下墓窖中僅存的雕像，是阿芙羅黛蒂的雕像。
What statue? I see no statue.	什麼雕像？我沒看見任何雕像。
It is quite dusty.	上頭積了不少塵土。
The apple made of solid gold was probably once a sacred object in a temple of the Goddess.	這顆純金打造的蘋果，昔日想必曾是女神神殿中的聖物。
The Seeress gave you the green apple, do you not remember?	女預言家給了你那顆青蘋果，你不記得了嗎？
She said that eating it would relieve all your hunger and thirst and give you renewed strength.	她說吃下它能解除你一切飢渴，並讓你重新恢復氣力。
Doves are a fertility symbol sacred to Aphrodite. But also it is widely believed that the soul becomes a dove at death and flies to heaven.	鴿子是阿芙羅黛蒂神聖的生育象徵。但也有人普遍相信，人死後靈魂會化為鴿子，飛往天堂。
The best I can tell you at the moment is that the stone dove you carry seems to be a stone dove.	此刻我能告訴你的，也不過是你身上那隻石鴿，看起來就是一隻石鴿。
These solid, musty rooms absorb your voice. You will have to search room by room.	這些厚實而霉味瀰漫的房間會吞沒你的聲音，你得一間一間地搜索。
Like the other dead souls in this place, he can no longer answer you.	如同此地其他亡魂一般，他已無法回應你了。
Do not expect him to answer. Even if he could hear you, he will not yet be healed and conscious.	別指望他會回應。就算他聽得見你，此刻也還未痊癒清醒。
There are poisonous.	牠們有毒。
No need. If you do not find a way out of these catacombs, you will BE dust.	不必如此。你若找不到走出這地下墓窖的路，終將化為塵土。
One disgusting old bone is quite enough.	一根噁心的老骨頭就已經夠了。
There are no loose bones here to pick up, Arthur, and there are rats lurking around the mummies.	此處並無散落的骨頭可拾取，亞瑟，木乃伊四周還潛伏著老鼠。
You don't have one.	你並未持有此物。
Not now. Keep your mind on what you are doing.	現在不行。專心在你正在做的事情上。
I cannot imagine a use for it....except for rats to gnaw upon.	我想不出它有什麼用處……除了讓老鼠啃食之外。
Disgusting. You are a king, not a ghoul.	噁心。你是一位國王，不是食屍鬼。
Nothing happens.	沒有任何反應。
Treat the dead with respect and caution. Especially in this place. And beware the rats.	對待亡者要心懷敬意，謹慎行事。在此地尤其如此。並且要提防老鼠。
It is a mummy. It has been dead for perhaps hundreds of years. Do try to show some sense.	那是一具木乃伊，死去恐怕已有數百年之久。還請你拿出點見識來。
Mummies are not known for their witty conversation.	木乃伊向來不以妙語如珠聞名。
It is good that no-one else is here to see you having a one-sided conversation with a poisonous rat.	幸好沒有旁人在此，看見你正對著一隻毒鼠自說自話。
Considering the danger of their bite, you are best to avoid these rats at all costs.	考量到牠們咬人的危險，你最好無論如何都避開這些老鼠。
They have plenty of bones to gnaw on.	牠們有大量的骨頭可以啃食。
That would be exceedingly foolish.	那將是極其愚蠢之舉。
You are already wearing it.	你已經戴著它了。
You do not have a medallion.	你並未持有六角星項鍊。
That would not be wise. It has a powerful warding spell upon it.	那並非明智之舉。它身上附有強力的護身法術。
Even King Midas could not eat a golden apple.	就連邁達斯王也無法吃下一顆金蘋果。
You have two apples to choose from. The green apple and the golden apple.	你有兩顆蘋果可以選擇：青蘋果與金蘋果。
Aye, but how?	正是，但該如何做到？
Clearly your challenge is to escape these catacombs. You must use your wits to discover the means.	顯然你面臨的難題，便是逃出這座地下墓窖。你必須運用機智，找出脫身之法。
There is no-one here who still desires mortal things.	此地已無人仍貪戀塵世之物。
That is the purpose of your mission. I pray you will succeed.	那正是你此行使命的目的。我祈求你能成功。
Arthur! Beware the rats! Any closer and you will be bitten!	亞瑟！當心那些老鼠！再靠近一步就會被咬傷！
Your strength is fading. The remorseless hand of Death draws near.	你的氣力正逐漸消逝。死神無情的手正步步逼近。
Another quest turned to dust, Another feast for the worms.	又一場任務化為塵土，又一頓供蛆蟲享用的盛宴。
I thank you, habib, but you need not pay me until we reach Jerusalem.	多謝你，朋友，但你不必現在付錢，等我們抵達耶路撒冷再說。
Do not lay hands upon me, foreigner!	休得對我動手，異鄉人！
Eh?  Dagger?  I have no dagger, habib.	嗯？匕首？我沒有匕首，朋友。
I did not bring one for this trip.  The desert is no threat to me.	這趟旅程我沒帶。沙漠對我構不成什麼威脅。
An odd trinket, of no use to me.  I would prefer money.	一件古怪的小玩意兒，對我毫無用處。我寧可要錢。
I would prefer money in exchange for my services.  We will discuss it at Jerusalem.	我提供服務，寧願換取金錢作為報酬。這事我們到耶路撒冷再談。
You have no waterskin?  A pity.  I need none, for I can well endure the desert.  You had best follow me closely to reach the water you need.	你沒有水袋？真可惜。我倒是不需要，畢竟我很能在沙漠裡耐得住。你最好緊跟著我，才能找到你需要的水。
Jabir means to kill you, Arthur!	賈比耳存心要殺你，亞瑟！
This name means nothing to me.	這個名字對我毫無意義。
You will see the walls of Jerusalem soon enough, but first you must have water.	你很快就能看見耶路撒冷的城牆，但在那之前，你得先有水才行。
Only one such as I knows the unmarked paths of the desert.	唯有像我這樣的人，才熟知沙漠裡那些不見標記的路徑。
Beware of mirages.  They will only lead you astray to your death.	當心海市蜃樓。它們只會將你引入歧途，步向死亡。
Your mule will last no longer than you without water.	沒有水，你的騾子撐不了比你更久。
Follow me.  I will lead you directly to water.	跟著我，我會直接帶你到水源那裡。
I know where every wadi is hidden.  Follow me.	每一處旱谷藏在哪裡，我都一清二楚。跟著我走。
Thief!  Robber!  You come seeking treasure, but you will find only death!	賊子！強盜！你前來尋找財寶，卻只會找到死亡！
Thief!  Dog of a bandit!  I should have known at once from your evil face!	賊子！強盜狗賊！看你那張凶惡的臉，我早該一眼看穿！
So! You have revealed yourself, enemy, as I knew you would!	哼！你終於露出真面目了，敵人，我早知道你會如此！
The power is mine!  Mine!  I will never share it!	這力量是我的！是我的！我絕不與人分享！
But you will never rob me, you devil!	但你休想搶得了我，你這惡魔！
Thief!  Robber!  You will never leave here alive!	賊子！強盜！你休想活著離開此地！
Greetings, stranger.  Welcome to Glastonbury Tor.	陌生人，你好。歡迎來到格列斯登伯利山。
Arthur.  The monk IS mad!	亞瑟，這僧侶果真是瘋了！
He does not answer yet. Try getting a bit closer.	他還沒有回應。試著再靠近一些。
I have made you welcome, though I wonder what your purpose may be, you with armour, shield and sword.	我已表明歡迎之意，只是好奇你此來所為何事——身披盔甲、手持盾牌與劍。
Well, la-dee-da.  And I am the Emperor of Rome.	喔，了不起啊。那我還是羅馬皇帝呢。
That rose smells of woman's magick.  I will not touch it.	那朵玫瑰散發著女人的魔法氣息，我不會去碰它。
I know that sleeve well.  It tells me that you are a great warrior, but less wise than you could be.	那袖子我再熟悉不過。它告訴我，你是位偉大的戰士，卻不如你原本能有的那般睿智。
Men in armour make me nervous. Go away.	身披盔甲的男人讓我心神不寧。走開。
As you can see, I am but an old, poor, helpless monk seeking enlightenment through solitude.  I am amazed you have passed the riddle stones, for your own face betrays no great intelligence.	如你所見，我不過是個年邁、貧困、無助的僧侶，藉獨處尋求開悟。你竟能通過謎語石的考驗，真教我驚訝——畢竟從你的面相看不出有多少才智。
They were once five poets, but the witch turned them to stone. Had you heard their poetry, you would understand why.	他們原是五位詩人，卻被女巫化為石頭。你若聽過他們的詩作，便會明白緣由。
I will only say that there is someone who wants it a great deal more than I.	我只能說，有人比我更想要它，想要得多。
The altar is ancient and has been here since the Druids worshipped upon this hill.	這座祭壇年代久遠，自德魯伊人在此山上禮拜的時代便已存在。
They tell wondrous secrets, but only to me.	它們訴說著奇妙的秘密，但只對我一人訴說。
I will never reveal my secrets!	我絕不會洩露我的秘密！
I cannot fathom what you mean, pilgrim.	我猜不透你的意思，朝聖者。
It is a ruined, desolate, lonely place. You cannot be enjoying it, so go away.	這是個殘破、荒涼、孤寂之地。你不可能樂在其中，走開吧。
I believe that I shall live forever.	我相信自己將會永生不死。
I believe the world revolves around my navel.	我相信這世界是繞著我的肚臍轉的。
I believe you are the nosiest man I ever met.	我相信你是我此生遇過最愛多管閒事的人。
Do you hear the chanting?  Aye, day and night they chant, the ghosts of the Old Ones.  I am never free of it.	你聽見那吟誦聲了嗎？正是，古代幽靈日夜不停地吟誦著，我從未能擺脫過它。
When I am left alone, I can seek enlightenment. If you wish to help me attain that exalted state, you will go away.	獨處之時，我才能追求開悟。你若真想助我達到那崇高的境界，就該離開。
I did not become a monk just so I could stand around answering your questions all day.	我出家為僧，可不是為了整天站在這裡回答你的問題。
I have no use for such a trinket.	這種小玩意兒，我用不著。
I should have expected no less from an armed barbarian.	從一個全副武裝的野蠻人身上，我本就不該有更高的期待。
You have been hacked to death by the Saracen.  Let us hope you will be a better swordsman in your next life.	你已被撒拉遜武士砍死。但願你來世能成為更出色的劍士。
Ah. The rat's poison has caught up with you. You have lost your desperate battle against time. Now, you shall have eternity to regret it.	啊，老鼠的毒液終究追上了你。你與時間的殊死搏鬥已然落敗。如今，你將有永恆的時光可以悔恨。
Now that the fight is over, the helmet also disappears.	如今戰鬥已然結束，頭盔也隨之消失。
You grow steadily weaker. Seek triumph from strategy, my king, as your strength wanes.	你正逐漸虛弱下去。吾王，趁你氣力尚未耗盡，當從謀略中尋求勝機。
Your death is near! You must win now or lose all.	你已命懸一線！此刻不勝，便將盡失所有。
Arthur, you are over-exerting yourself. Slow down, or you will lack the strength to fight.	亞瑟，你已過度耗力。放慢下來，否則你將無力再戰。
Your sword feels as heavy as lead. Defend yourself with your shield until some of your strength returns.	你的劍沉如鉛塊。且以盾牌自守，靜候氣力回復幾分。
Excaliber flashes in your skilled hands. Victory is imminent!	聖劍在你嫻熟的手中閃耀光芒，勝利已近在眼前！
The Saracen weakens under your skillful attack. Keep fighting like this and you will be victorious.	撒拉遜武士在你精湛的攻勢下逐漸虛弱。照這樣打下去，你必將獲勝。
Your skull is cracked, Your body dead, Your brains are gone, Your spirit fled, The Monk played tag Upon your head.	你的顱骨碎裂，你的軀體已亡，你的腦漿四散，你的魂魄已散，僧侶在你頭頂，戲耍了一場。
Arrghh...in vino veritas...	啊啊……酒後吐真言……
Well done, Arthur!	做得好，亞瑟！
We are the Old Ones and you have killed the monk, our servant, the only servant we have had for centuries.	我們是古代幽靈，你殺了那僧侶——我們的僕人，數百年來，他是我們僅有的一位僕人。
You must take his place.  You will never leave here, unless you can appease us for this loss.	你必須取代他的位置。除非你能平息我們因此喪失而生的怒火，否則你將永遠困在此地。
In this section of the temple there are four broken and fallen pillars.	神殿的這一區域，有四根斷裂倒塌的柱子。
In this section of the Temple there are three broken pillars and an indentation where a fourth pillar once stood.	神殿的這一區域，有三根斷裂的柱子，以及第四根柱子原本立足處留下的凹痕。
These steps must be the only remnant of the original door to the Temple. At the threshold there is a lunar spiral engraved in the marble.	這些石階想必是神殿原本大門僅存的遺跡。門檻的大理石上，刻著一道月亮螺紋。
There are also three broken pillars and an indentation where a fourth pillar once stood.	此處同樣有三根斷裂的柱子，以及第四根柱子原本立足處留下的凹痕。
An interesting idea, if one can find a way to do so.	這想法有趣，前提是得找到辦法做到。
You cannot see beyond the walls surrounding the Temple except for a glimpse of tree tops and tiled roofs in the distance.	神殿四周高牆之外，你什麼也看不見，只能瞥見遠方的樹梢與瓦頂一角。
No part of the Temple's roof remains. Only the sky arches overhead.	神殿的屋頂已蕩然無存，唯有天空在頭頂上方拱起。
The floor of the Temple is made of marble, weathered from the ages and invaded by weeds.	神殿的地面以大理石鋪成，歷經歲月風化，如今已被雜草侵佔。
You will never see her again.	你將再也見不到她了。
She will reveal herself to you only when she is ready.	唯有等她準備好了，才會向你現身。
This part of the Temple of Aphrodite is surrounded by high walls without doors or windows. There is no way out from this direction.	阿芙羅黛蒂神殿的這一部分，四周高牆環繞，既無門也無窗，這個方向無路可通。
By all that is sacred, King Arthur, go where the dove leads you and forget all else!	以一切神聖之名起誓，亞瑟王，隨鴿子引領你的方向前行，其餘一概拋諸腦後！
Arthur, pay attention! A powerful foe awaits you. This is no time to play at being Sampson.	亞瑟，打起精神來！強敵正等著你。此刻不是逞英雄學參孫的時候。
The pedestal is immovable.	這座基座紋風不動。
I sense that the power of the Goddess keeps you from treading there, where once her holy of holies must have been kept.	我感覺到女神的力量，正阻止你踏入那處——那裡想必曾是她的至聖之所。
Die, infidel	去死吧，異教徒
I was going to make a remark about using your brains, Arthur, but since I see they are all over the ground, along with your blood, heart, kidneys, liver, lungs and intestines, I guess there is no point.	我原想說幾句要你多動動腦子的話，亞瑟，可我見你的腦漿已灑滿一地，連同你的血、心臟、腎臟、肝臟、肺臟與腸子，看來也沒什麼意義了。
YOU MAY NOT PASS THIS WAY!  Do not annoy us, infidel.	你不得從此路通行！休得惹惱我們，異教徒。
What utterly stupid animals they are!	牠們真是群徹頭徹尾的蠢畜生！
Aye, the woman is herding away her sheep.  What utterly stupid animals they are.	正是，那女人正把她的羊群趕開。牠們真是群徹頭徹尾的蠢畜生。
She shows not the least interest in talking to you.	她絲毫沒有興趣跟你說話。
Sheep are the most brainless creatures upon the face of the earth.  That does not bode well for someone who wants to talk to them.	羊是這世上最沒腦子的生物。這對想跟牠們交談的人來說，可不是什麼好兆頭。
You missed.  A large, heavy sword is not the best method for this, perhaps.	你揮空了。一把又大又重的劍，或許並非對付這個的最佳方式。
Fast little devils, are they not?	這些小傢伙動作真快，不是嗎？
If you mean the legged creature that scurried past, it was a lizard.	你若是指那隻疾竄而過、生著腿的生物，那是一隻蜥蜴。
It is not worth the effort...unless you are well and truly desperate enough.	這不值得費這番功夫……除非你已當真走投無路。
This lizard is moving too fast for you.	這隻蜥蜴動作太快，你追不上。
The lizard is too far away.	這隻蜥蜴離得太遠了。
Aye, you see Launcelot making love to Gwenhyver, but it is only a mirage, a torment from your own mind.	正是，你看見蘭斯洛特與昆海兒繾綣纏綿，但那不過是海市蜃樓，是你自己心中生出的折磨。
